# EcoSuit SOLO — Earth → Moon → Earth, no spacecraft
**The suit is the vehicle.**
This is the composition of that object, not a way to hide a capsule behind a plastron.

A 210–250 kg worn ER-1 article cannot do this. The rocket equation and Earth entry both refuse.
SOLO is therefore a **person-shaped stage**: exo + plates + hatch + the tanks, engines, shield, and days of LS that used to live in other vehicles.

---

## 0. Verdict on “just the suit”

| Job | Worn ER-1 (~230 kg) | SOLO closed system |
|---|---|---|
| 15–16 km/s Earth → lunar surface | No | Multi-stage tanks you are wearing |
| Lunar stay + TEI | No | More tanks |
| 11 km/s Earth interface | No. Chest radius is a blowtorch | A real heat shield with a usable radius, then chutes or a landing burn |
| Walk after landing | Yes | Only if the stages have been dropped |

Hydrolox, Δv ≈ 18 km/s propulsive (out + Moon ascent + TEI, Earth landing on a shield):

    m0 / mf = exp(Δv / ve) ≈ exp(18 / 4.4) ≈ 60

If “dry” were 250 kg, wet mass ≈ 15 t — and that dry number is a lie, because the tanks and engines to move 15 t are themselves tonnes. Closed SOLO sits in the **tens of tonnes wet** class, not the backpack class. Cold gas and 2600 am ABH-in-the-sternum do not change this.

ABH-2600-REAL in the chest remains FAIL-CLOSED (12 g at 1 m, 132 g at 0.3 m). Ice does not feed 2.6 fm.

