## 1. What SOLO is made of (the whole object)

Three discarded stages + one reentry body that still looks like the suit.
STAGE 0   Earth liftoff / max-q / to ~2–3 km/s     drop STAGE 1   to LEO / TLI energy                       drop STAGE 2   TLI + midcourse + LOI + landing           drop or keep as lunar pack CORE      crew + HUT + plates + shield + TEI + LS   this is the “suit” that comes home

Single-stage Earth→Moon→Earth in one set of tanks: mass explodes. SOLO stages or it does not exist.

---

## 2. CORE composition (the thing that lands on Earth)

Same layer order as MK.I, then the vehicle parts glued to the dorsal lattice and the windward OML.

### 2.1 Crew shell
- Rear-entry HUT, step-in hatch, dual seals
- BLAD + REST + LCVG + helmet / slit visor
- EXO-TI / Ti-6Al-4V ELI spine, yoke, hatch ring
- SEAs hip/knee, cable-SEAs arm/ankle, clutches fail-OPEN
- CUP-SM analog only (≤ 8 kg). No REAL core

### 2.2 Windward OML (this is now a heat shield, not a fashion tile)
Earth interface ~11 km/s. Stagnation heating on a human-chest radius is unsurvivable if the chest *is* the nose.

SOLO therefore cheats geometry, not physics:
- Reentry attitude: feet- or pack-first, **effective nose radius metres, not centimetres**
- Windward stack, outside → in:
  1. Ablator or HRSI-class tile / PICA-class / or ceramic-hemp only as isolator under a real ablator
  2. Strain isolator (HEMP / PI or metal honeycomb)
  3. Structural skin (Ti-6Al-4V or Grade C 718)
  4. Insulation
  5. Pressure shell
- Leeward: CER-W / metal radiator, pack, hatch
- Visor closed, slit capped, V-EBM inhibited
- After plasma: jettison or keep charred windward scales; they are not walk-off tiles

CER-B alone on a 0.3 m sternum is not this shield.

### 2.3 Home-stage propulsion (TEI + lunar ascent if Stage 2 is gone)
- Storables or hydrolox on the dorsal lattice and pelvic yoke
- Engines on the yoke / pack corners, never on hemp cores
- T/W_lunar ≥ 2 if this core must leave the Moon by itself
- T/W_Earth of the **CORE alone** is irrelevant; Stage 0 owns the pad
- RCS on pack corners for entry attitude

### 2.4 Earth landing after the shield
Pick one; both are part of SOLO, not a waiting spacecraft:
- Drogue + mains out of the pack, or
- Residual propulsive touchdown

Splash or dirt. Hatch opens. Step-out.

### 2.5 Life support (no cabin to hide in)
The CORE carries the whole cruise.

| Item | Order |
|---|---|
| Duration | 6–10 days out + stay + 3–6 days home (free-return class) |
| O₂ / N₂ | Tanks on pack / yoke, not a 8 h EVA bottle |
| CO₂ | Regenerable or a canister mass that is a stage by itself |
| Water | Drink + LCVG + radiator loop |
| Power | Fuel cell or batteries sized in kWh-days, not EVA-hours |
| Thermal | Radiators on leeward scales; entry is a heat-capacity + ablator problem |
| Waste | In-suit |

This LS mass is why “dry = 250 kg” never happens.

