## 4. Materials bill (SOLO CORE + what it drops)

**Crew / structure**
- Ti-6Al-4V ELI exo, hatch, yoke
- 718 / 625 cup, engine bells, hot fittings
- A286 or Ti captives
- S-glass / PI where dielectric

**Faces**
- Windward: ablator or HRSI-class on a metre-class radius aeroshell that happens to be attached to the suit
- Walk-off acreage: CER-B/W + hemp core **or** Grade A FeNi scales (not the windward nose)
- Leeward: CER-W / radiator

**Core / isolator**
- HEMP-W/U/M + MAT-P + ADH-F on walk-off plates
- Metal honeycomb under the shield
- No hemp in cup, bells, or shield bond to structure without a fire line

**Propellants (the mass)**
- Stage 0–1: LOX/LH2 or LOX/CH4
- CORE TEI: storables preferred (no 6-day cryo boiloff on a backpack)
- RCS: GN₂ or MMH/NTO class
- Ice particulates: working fluid on a radiator loop only — not a horizon feed

**Reject on SOLO**
- Single 230 kg garment
- Sternum ABH-2600-REAL
- FTL as a Δv source
- “Chest tiles = Apollo heat shield”
- Unclutched harmonic joints during 6 g
- Suit O₂ as a muscle gas
- One tank set for 18 km/s

