## 6. Sequence with no other spacecraft

1. Step-in on a stand that is also the pad hold-down. SEAs OPEN. HV off.
2. Hatch, helmet. CORE is already inside Stage 0/1.
3. Stage 0: liftoff, max-q, drop.
4. Stage 1: orbital / TLI energy, drop.
5. Stage 2: cruise burns, LOI, land on yoke gear. Dust protocol.
6. EVA: CORE walks in plates. SEAs impedance. V-EBM only in hard vac.
7. Leave Moon: Stage 2 leftovers or CORE engines. T/W_lunar ≥ 2.
8. TEI from CORE tanks.
9. Earth interface: CORE only. Windward shield into the corridor. Attitude from pack RCS.
10. Chutes or last burn. Hatch. Step-out. Walk-off composition is ER-1 again.

No chase vehicle. No waiting capsule. The dropped tanks are debris unless you plan recovery.

